  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-2304" textLabel="CYP83A1 monooxygenase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-2304" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="475" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>CYP83A1 metabolizes aldoximes derived from chain-elongated methionine. The Km for these aliphatic aldoximes is in the range of 20 to 150 uM |CITS: [12970475]|. Both CYP83A1 and CYP83B1 metabolize phenylacetaldoxime. However phenylacetaldoxime is a better substrate for CYP83B1. The Km of CYP83A1 for phenylacetaldoxime is 3-fold higher than that of CYP83B1. The catalytic efficiency (Kcat/Km) of CYP83B1 is 6 times higher than that of CYP83A1 |CITS: [12970475]|. The reaction is thought to involve a carbon-sulfur lyase to form the thiohydroximate from the intermediate alkylthiohydroximate |CITS: [12049923]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-2304" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP83A1" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT4G13770-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33857, RXN-17793, RXN-17800, RXN-17802, RXN-17804, RXN-17806, RXN-17808, RXN-17810" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="8" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11158532" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12970475" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11553739" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12049923" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-2303" textLabel="CYP79F2 monooxygenase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-2303" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="555" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>Both CYP79F1 and CYP79F2 are involved in methionine-derived aliphatic glucosinolates biosynthesis. CYP79F1 can metabolize homo, di, tri, tetra, penta, and hexahomomethionine to their corresponding aldoximes, and has higher substrate specificity for di or trihomomethionine. CYP79F2, on the other hand, can only metabolize penta and hexahomomethionine. CYP79F1 knockout plants lack short-chain aliphatic glucosinolates, whereas, CYP79F2 knockouts have reduced level of long-chain aliphatic glucosinolates but unchanged level of short chain glucosinolates. CYP79F1 is highly expressed in rosette, stem and silique. CYP79F2 is highly expressed in root.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-2303" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="CYP79F2" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT1G16400-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33135, RXN-33134, RXN-33133, RXN-33132, RXN-2845, RXN-12478, RXN-12477" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="7" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005783" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCO-ER" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="62." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="62." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12609033" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
